{"assets":["/statement-assets/0c91ad84d460bbe37f206b10050a9b46336822cc5a47c61a9c7c0baaea1088ea.png","/statement-assets/ca0cafe5e089cb3df7d490df8fad0015412ffe6941b0249e2dfa83e97a0da70a.png","/statement-assets/88d00d80824d8c91f654d91376de1194a201263a2716db77bf93ccae7d535db3.png","/statement-assets/e800e8b616677926e656648d158b5779bf82a839d6803e5adff3cd274ec0ef27.png","/statement-assets/a13f4c1dd0b118b5636fe91f6a4d7cd261c09b940302620167ae4254b428e212.png","/statement-assets/41758d5fe8f66a39ec7ca007e142ec63c31e969234de413d53c9326d3aa61277.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1741","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Masha and a Beautiful Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The girl named Masha was walking in the forest and found a complete binary tree of height $$$n$$$ and a permutation $$$p$$$ of length $$$m=2^n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A complete binary tree of height $$$n$$$ is a rooted tree such that every vertex except the leaves has exactly two sons, and the length of the path from the root to any of the leaves is $$$n$$$. The picture below shows the complete binary tree for $$$n=2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A permutation is an array consisting of $$$n$$$ different integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. For example, [$$$2,3,1,5,4$$$] is a permutation, but [$$$1,2,2$$$] is not ($$$2$$$ occurs twice), and [$$$1,3,4$$$] is also not a permutation ($$$n=3$$$, but there is $$$4$$$ in the array)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's enumerate $$$m$$$ leaves of this tree from left to right. The leaf with the number $$$i$$$ contains the value $$$p_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le m$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$n = 2$$$, $$$p = [3, 1, 4, 2]$$$, the tree will look like this:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/0c91ad84d460bbe37f206b10050a9b46336822cc5a47c61a9c7c0baaea1088ea.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Masha considers a tree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beautiful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the values in its leaves are ordered from left to right in increasing order."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one operation, Masha can choose any non-leaf vertex of the tree and swap its left and right sons (along with their subtrees)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if Masha applies this operation to the root of the tree discussed above, it will take the following form:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/ca0cafe5e089cb3df7d490df8fad0015412ffe6941b0249e2dfa83e97a0da70a.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help Masha understand if she can make a tree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beautiful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in a certain number of operations. If she can, then output the minimum number of operations to make the tree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beautiful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In each test case, the first line contains an integer $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le m \\le 262144$$$), which is a power of two  — the size of the permutation $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$m$$$ integers: $$$p_1, p_2, \\dots, p_m$$$ ($$$1 \\le p_i \\le m$$$) — the permutation $$$p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$m$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$3 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case in a separate line, print the minimum possible number of operations for which Masha will be able to make the tree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beautiful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if this is not possible."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n8\n6 5 7 8 4 3 1 2\n4\n3 1 4 2\n1\n1\n8\n7 8 4 3 1 2 6 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n-1\n0\n-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the first test."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, you can act like this (the vertex to which the operation is applied at the current step is highlighted in purple): "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/88d00d80824d8c91f654d91376de1194a201263a2716db77bf93ccae7d535db3.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e800e8b616677926e656648d158b5779bf82a839d6803e5adff3cd274ec0ef27.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a13f4c1dd0b118b5636fe91f6a4d7cd261c09b940302620167ae4254b428e212.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/41758d5fe8f66a39ec7ca007e142ec63c31e969234de413d53c9326d3aa61277.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" It can be shown that it is impossible to make a tree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beautiful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in fewer operations."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, it can be shown that it is impossible to make a tree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beautiful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, the tree is already "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beautiful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1741D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1741/problem/D"}